The probability density function of evaporation $$E$$ on any day during a year in a watershed is given by 
$$$f\left( E \right) = \left\{ {\matrix{
   {{1 \over 5}} &amp; {0 \le E \le 5\,mm/day}  \cr 
   0 &amp; {otherwise}  \cr 

 } } \right.$$$
<br>The probability that $$E$$ lies in between $$2$$ and $$4$$ $$mm/day$$ in the watershed is (in decimal) _______.

